  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "\"shake\" covers moving something on purpose (*shake the bottle*), shaking you cannot control (*my hands shook*), and emotional shock (*the news shook her*). Many languages use separate verbs.",
    "grammar": null,
    "culture": "In English-speaking countries shaking your head usually means *no*; head movements can mean different things in other places, so check the gesture before translating. A handshake is a common greeting in business.",
